CE carries the relation type,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and the Artifacts Agent pane filters on `relation:`, `linked:`, and[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`artifact:`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]14[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]artifact_link_durability_and_derivation.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/artifact_link_durability_and_derivation.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-tw[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-tw/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A rebuild may delete only what it can prove was deleted[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]index-durability[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]index-durability: make `preview_aggregate` carry forward prior rows [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whose owning companion is not visible in this workspace, make `link rm` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prune the aggregate unconditionally, add a cross-workspace [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconciliation sweep gated on agent publication, and add doctor counters[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that make future index divergence loud.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Audited reads become durable and publish with the agent's [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]commits[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]read-outbox[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-durability[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]read-outbox: add a machine-local, replayable artifact-link outbox so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase artifact read` stops leaving its row uncommitted, and drain it at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stitch publication and from housekeeping, publishing an agent-endpoint [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row only once that agent resolves as published.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A bead in either endpoint position gets its event[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bead-endpoints[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-durability[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead-endpoints: teach the sase-core bead link wire a direction, fire [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`_upsert_bead` when the bead is the target as well as the source, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]backfill the endpoint events one-sided writes never produced, and make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase artifact create --bead` write a typed link with `reference_added` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kept as a legacy alias.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Links follow renames instead of dangling[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rename-following[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-durability[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rename-following: consume git rename detection in the sidecar link [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh so a moved artifact carries its rows and its `links/` companion,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]then repair every dangling ref and orphaned companion the research [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]workflow has already created.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Relation semantics, `derived` projection class, and a way to [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]read them[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]relation-registry[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]relation-registry: settle `plan implements bead` in the registry with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]direction, worked examples, and recommended endpoint kinds; expose it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through `sase artifact link relation list|show` and completions; and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]give `derived` a projection class so host-derived semantic edges render.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One derivation module behind one flag[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]derivation-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after relation-registry, bead-endpoints[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]derivation-core: add the Textual-free derivation module that turns facts[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE already owns into `derived` rows -- research-swarm `__a`/`__b` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lineage and plan `bead_id:` frontmatter -- behind a beta feature flag, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with no call sites yet.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Derive at creation, on sidecar commit, and in the hourly sweep[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]derivation-hooks[dim] · [dim][/dim]after derivation-core, rename-following, read-outbox[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]derivation-hooks: call the derivation module from `sase plan propose` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and `sase artifact create`, from the sidecar commit path for artifacts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that land another way, and from a new `sase_chop_artifact_link_backfill`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chop in the hourly housekeeping bucket that runs the retroactive sweep.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The citation channel stops starving[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]citations[dim] · [dim][/dim]after derivation-hooks[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]citations: derive `agent cites plan` from the archived prompt's own [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]header block and resolve prose sidecar paths in published prompts into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`cites` rows, while explicitly holding the plan `AGENTS`/`COMMITS` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sections out of the graph.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Run the RELATED: note backfill[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]notes-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bead-endpoints[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes-migration: verify `sase artifact link migrate-notes --apply` on a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scratch bead tree, correct its stale help text, and run it for real to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]convert the 269 auto-convertible `RELATED:` notes into typed related [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]links.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Finish the `links:` frontmatter inlet as an authoring path[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]frontmatter-inlet[dim] · [dim][/dim]after derivation-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]frontmatter-inlet: give the orphaned Rust `links:` parser its production[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]caller so an author can declare links in plan frontmatter, and make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]consumption remove the inlet so it never becomes a second editable copy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of the row.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make every audited read a discovery moment[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]read-payoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-durability, relation-registry[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]read-payoff: print a one-line typed neighborhood footer from `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact read`, warn when the artifact being read is superseded, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expand exactly one typed hop when a launch prompt cites an artifact.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE stops flattening the relation type[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ace-fidelity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after relation-registry[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace-fidelity: carry relation slug, directional label, description, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]origin, and use count from the aggregate row into ACE's relation rail [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of collapsing every edge to `links`/`linked_by`, and add a typed[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]link action with a required reason.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]`relation:`, `linked:`, and `artifact:` on the Agent pane[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]agent-pane-filters[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-durability, ace-fidelity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-pane-filters: join artifact-link facets onto the agent catalog [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]query entry and declare the three link fields in the agents profile so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both the Artifacts Agent pane and `sase agent search` can filter on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]them.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The judgment tier, the flag removal, and the two workflow [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]lines[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]suggest-and-close[dim] · [dim][/dim]after citations, notes-migration, frontmatter-inlet,[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]read-payoff, agent-pane-filters[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]suggest-and-close: add `sase artifact link suggest` over hard evidence [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]only, remove the derivation featur